WHAT THIS IS
============
The source code of Refract is published so that anyone can READ and AUDIT it.
That transparency is part of the product: Refract processes microphone audio,
screen content and personal documents on your machine, and you should be able
to verify that it does not send them anywhere.

Publishing the source is NOT a grant of rights. This is source-available
software, not open source.

WHAT YOU MAY DO
===============
1. Read, study and audit this source code.
2. Run the official builds distributed by the copyright holder.
3. Quote short excerpts for review, teaching, security research or commentary,
   with attribution.

